WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.125
At last the Caterpillar spoke to Alice.

2
00:00:05.126 --> 00:00:10.271
"Who are you?" he asked in a sleepy voice.

3
00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:14.252
This was not the best way to start a conversation.

4
00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:18.836
Alice replied rather shyly, "I hardly know, sir.

5
00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:22.763
At least I know who I was when I got up this morning.

6
00:00:22.764 --> 00:00:26.256
But I've changed several times since then."

7
00:00:26.257 --> 00:00:33.414
"What do you mean by that? Explain yourself," the Caterpillar said.

8
00:00:33.415 --> 00:00:38.756
Alice tried to be polite even though the Caterpillar seemed rather rude.

9
00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:41.795
"I'm afraid I can't put it more clearly, sir.

10
00:00:41.796 --> 00:00:45.447
Being so many different sizes in one day is confusing." "No,

11
00:00:45.448 --> 00:00:49.393
it isn't." "Perhaps

12
00:00:49.394 --> 00:00:53.334
you haven't had the chance to find that out yet," Alice said. "When

13
00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:58.310
you change into a butterfly, you'll probably feel quite strange." "I

14
00:00:58.311 --> 00:01:02.781
will not," the Caterpillar said. "You

15
00:01:02.782 --> 00:01:08.290
may feel differently than I do," Alice said, still trying to be polite. "But

16
00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:12.832
turning into a butterfly would feel very strange to me." "You!"

17
00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:17.644
The Caterpillar's voice was full of scorn. "Who

18
00:01:17.645 --> 00:01:21.038
are you ?"

19
00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:26.132
And that brought them right back to the beginning of their conversation.

20
00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:29.949
Alice felt annoyed by the Caterpillar's remarks.

21
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:34.595
She stood as tall as she could and looked straight at him.

22
00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:40.787
"I think you should tell me who you are first."

23
00:01:40.788 --> 00:01:43.680
"Why?"

24
00:01:43.681 --> 00:01:48.637
This was another puzzling question that Alice couldn't answer.

25
00:01:48.638 --> 00:01:53.538
The Caterpillar was in such a bad mood that she wanted to leave.

26
00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:57.770
She started to walk away.

27
00:01:57.771 --> 00:02:01.475
"Come back!" the Caterpillar called after her.

28
00:02:01.475 --> 00:02:06.657
"I have something important to say!"

29
00:02:06.657 --> 00:02:13.627
This sounded interesting, so Alice walked back to the mushroom and waited for him to speak.

30
00:02:13.628 --> 00:02:24.217
"Don't lose your temper," the Caterpillar said.

31
00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:32.033
"Is that all?" Alice couldn't believe how angry he made her feel. "No."

32
00:02:32.034 --> 00:02:34.303
For

33
00:02:34.304 --> 00:02:39.808
a few minutes, the Caterpillar sat silently, ignoring Alice. She

34
00:02:39.809 --> 00:02:45.173
was going to leave, but she really had nothing else to do. So

35
00:02:45.174 --> 00:02:48.473
she decided to wait. Perhaps

36
00:02:48.474 --> 00:02:54.596
the Caterpillar would have something interesting to say after all. Finally

37
00:02:54.597 --> 00:02:57.427
he spoke to her again. "So

38
00:02:57.428 --> 00:03:03.265
you think you've changed?" "Oh,

39
00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:08.109
yes," Alice said, happy that he was listening at last. "First

40
00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.703
I'm bigger, and then I'm smaller. I

41
00:03:10.704 --> 00:03:14.129
don't stay the same size for more than a few minutes." The

42
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.980
Caterpillar looked Alice up and down. "What

43
00:03:17.981 --> 00:03:22.576
size do you want to be?" "I

44
00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:28.756
don't really care. I just don't like changing so often, you know?" "No,

45
00:03:28.757 --> 00:03:33.384
I don't know," the Caterpillar replied. Alice

46
00:03:33.385 --> 00:03:35.725
said nothing. She'd

47
00:03:35.726 --> 00:03:41.919
never met such a disagreeable creature, and she was losing her temper. The

48
00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:48.790
Caterpillar interrupted her thoughts. "Are you happy now?" "I'd

49
00:03:48.791 --> 00:03:54.851
like to be larger because three inches is such a horrible size." "Three

50
00:03:54.852 --> 00:03:58.922
inches is the perfect height!" The

51
00:03:58.923 --> 00:04:07.571
Caterpillar stretched upright as he spoke, showing that he was exactly three inches high. "But

52
00:04:07.572 --> 00:04:12.372
I'm not used to it!" Alice moaned. "You'll

53
00:04:12.373 --> 00:04:17.635
get used to it in time," said the Caterpillar. Alice waited,

54
00:04:17.636 --> 00:04:23.113
hoping the Caterpillar would say something more. Eventually he

55
00:04:23.114 --> 00:04:31.901
yawned twice, and shook himself. Then he

56
00:04:31.902 --> 00:04:39.842
got down from the mushroom. "One side

57
00:04:39.843 --> 00:04:47.412
makes you grow taller," the Caterpillar said, crawling through the grass. "And the

58
00:04:47.413 --> 00:04:52.147
other side makes you smaller." Alice wondered

59
00:04:52.148 --> 00:04:56.625
what in the world he was talking about. "One side

60
00:04:56.626 --> 00:05:02.184
of what ? The other side of what ?" she thought.

61
00:05:02.185 --> 00:05:08.643
"Of the mushroom!" The Caterpillar replied as if Alice had asked her questions aloud.

62
00:05:08.643 --> 00:05:18.903
And in another moment, he was out of sight.

